# Pairs with NoLostWrite. An export records the head it opened at as its cut
# but holds a shorter prefix, so the cut overstates what it contains and a
# rewind to the retained floor after a covered settle leaves a hole.
MODULE: NoLostWriteTrustedExportHoldsLess
TARGET: NoLostWrite
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a trusted export holds less than the cut it records, so a covered settle loses writes
PERTURBS: Export

--- FIND
          /\ t => s = head
--- REPLACE
          \* MUTATION: a trusted export may hold less than its cut.
          /\ t => s <= head
--- END